{"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to politely disagree with a colleague."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alternative "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " another way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have an alternative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to offer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to present something to someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:<span class=\"strong\">Joe</span>: Can I offer you a drink? <br /> <span class =\"strong\">Nancy</span>: Sure!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "opinion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "what someone thinks "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In my opinion, he is the best teacher!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "staff "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of employees"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:The staff work from 9 a.m to 5 p.m."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to benefit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to receive an advantage, use with from"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can benefit from more staff meetings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "agreement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a situation when two people have the same opinion "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bill and I are in agreement about this."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "paragraph "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of sentences together with one idea "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The first paragraph is about my opinion."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ASAP "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "as soon as possible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Get back to me ASAP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le08ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Simple Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use the Present Simple to talk about facts and usual actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form the negative, use do / does not  before the verb. </br>Do not add s to the verb when used with he, she, it.</br> Pay attention to the short form. It's used in talking.</br></br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form a yes/no question, use do/does and change the word order like this:         \tDo / Does + subject + verb </br>Do not add s to the verb with he, she, it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Evening work is difficult."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I don't know if the company can afford it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do the employees work a lot of overtime?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a letter to your boss. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content